  "text": "Board of Elections | Warren County, NC\nSkip to Main Content\nCreate a Website Account\n- Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nSearch\nGovernment\nDepartments\nServices\nCommunity\nHow Do I...\nHome\nGovernment\nBoards & Commissions\nD - F\nBoard of Elections\nBoard of Elections\nLast Content Update:\nLast week\nResponsibilities\nThis board conducts county elections. Broadly, the Warren County of Elections has responsibility for conducting Federal, State, and local elections held within the County. The North Carolina General Statutes Chapter 163 and other applicable statutes govern the Warren County Board of Elections. The department has responsibility for the management of the voter registration information within Warren County.\n2026 GENERAL ELECTION INFORMATION\nThe 2026 Election will be Tuesday, November 3, 2026. Please see below for important dates and other relevant information.\nSeptember 4: Absentee ballots mailed to eligible voters who submitted a request form.\nOctober 9 at 5PM: Voter registration deadline.\nOctober 15: In-person early voting begins.\nOctober 20 at 5 PM: Deadline to request an absentee ballot.\nOctober 31 at 3 PM: In-person early voting ends.\nNovember 3: Election Day. Polling places are open from 6:30 a.m. to 7:30 p.m.\nNovember 3 at 7:30 PM.: Deadline to submit absentee ballots\nNovember 10 @ 12:00 PM: Deadline to show acceptable ID.\nBoard Members\nMembers are appointed by the state.\nMembers\nRoles\nBetty Mazor - Republican\nChairman\nHenry Durham, Jr. - Democrat\nMember\nJames Roberts - Democrat\nMember\nWalter Hundley - Republican\nSecretary\nJoanne Thompson - Republican\nMember\nResources\nFor more information on the North Carolina Board of Elections, please visit the\nstate website\n.\nCalendar\nSat, Oct. 17\n(CLOSED) EARLY VOTING HOURS FOR THE NOVEMBER 3, 2026 GENERAL ELECTION\nSun, Oct. 18\n(CLOSED)EARLY VOTING HOURS FOR THE NOVEMBER 3, 2026 GENERAL ELECTION\nMon, Oct. 19\nEARLY VOTING HOURS FOR THE NOVEMBER 3, 2026 GENERAL ELECTION\nView All Events\n/Calendar.aspx\nContact Us\nBoard of Elections\nPhysical Address\nView Map\n309 N Main Street\nAnnex Bldg.\nWarrenton\n,\nNC\n27589\n309 N Main Street Annex Bldg. Warrenton NC 27589\nDirections\nMailing Address\nP.O. Box 803\nWarrenton\n,\nNC\n27589\nPhone:\n252-257-2114\nFax: 252-257-5232\nHours\nMonday - Friday\n8:30 a.m. - 5 p.m.\nDirectory\nBoard of Elections Notices and Documents\nBuffer Zones\nFVAP - UOCAVA\nGENERAL ELECTION 2026 - RESOLUTION (PDF)\nNOTICE - LOGIC AND ACCURACY (L and A) TESTING (2026 GENERAL ELECTION)\nUOCAVA Notice\nHow to Register\nVoter Registration Form\nMAT Team - Nursing Home Requests for Voter Assistance\nBecome an Election Official\n2026 General Election (Candidate Detail List)\nPrecinct Locations\nWarren County Voting Precincts Map\nGIS\nHuman Resources\nTax Administration\nRegister of Deeds\nSheriff's Office\nPlanning/Zoning/Code\nContact Us\nWarren County\n602 W Ridgeway Street\nWarrenton, NC 27589\nPopular Links\nGIS\nCounty Budget\nNow Hiring\nDeed Search\nPay My Tax Bill\nBuilding Permits\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nSite Links\nHome\nSite Map\nContact Us\nAccessibility\nCopyright Notices\n/QuickLinks.aspx\nGovernment Websites by\nCivicPlus\u00ae\nLoading\nLoading\nDo Not Show Again\nClose\nArrow Left\nArrow Right\n[]\nSlideshow Left Arrow\nSlideshow Right Arrow",
